# The vendored tree is stored byte for byte as upstream has it. The root's `text=auto eol=lf`
# would otherwise convert any CRLF file upstream adds, and vendor-xterm-net.ps1 -Verify compares
# bytes: one converted file would fail it on every machine. (Upstream is LF today, except
# src/XTerm.NET/Common/Charsets.cs, which carries CR bytes git already treats as binary.)
XTerm.NET/** -text

# The patches are git mail; leave their bytes alone too.
XTerm.NET.patches/*.patch -text
